 "notes": "Claude first pass (exemplar record, pH 7.07). Recurrent deep decels (nadirs 65-85, depths 40-60) roughly one per contraction for 80 min. Blind morphology read: onset-to-nadir is 7-34s (abrupt by NICHD) with fast recoveries and nadirs at or just after the contraction peak (+0..+20s) - typed variable throughout, i.e. the recurrent-variable reading, NOT trains of early/late; exceptions d12 (o2n 38s, nadir +43s, slow recovery -> late) and d19 (o2n 34s, nadir +17s, gradual -> early, borderline). d27-d32 carry the UC flag (toco lost after -8). Second stage: between-decel FHR sits at 100-110 for minutes, so the baseline fall to ~105 is genuine, not detector error. Two detector misses added there: dm69 -17.15..-16.82 (nadir 72, on c62) and dm70 -14.4..-13.95 (nadir 78, on c64), both abrupt -> variable. Quiet zone -54..-41 has no qualifying decels (dips <15 bpm).",
